\paragraph{A fourth trajectory: CIVO-induced persistent value collapse.}
Obs-decoder SGS seed~3 (exp\_025) exhibits a trajectory not observed in the untreated seeds: healthy through 105K ($\nve < 1.0\times$, eval 818.6), CIVO onset at 135K ($\nve = 5.47\times$, eval 67.0), followed by evaluation recovery (590.2 at 215K, 64\% of baseline) but persistent value collapse ($\nve = 0.14\times$, value mean 80.6). The critic undershoots after the CIVO episode, suggesting that CIVO-induced representational damage may be irreversible even when the policy partially recovers. This contrasts with transient CIVO (seed~2, 009b), where both value and evaluation recover jointly, and with full collapse (seed~1, 008d), where neither recovers. The pattern adds a fourth post-CIVO outcome---policy recovery with critic damage---to the three documented in Table~\ref{tab:post_civo}.

