\paragraph{Obs-decoder SGS induces universal value collapse.}
Beyond failing to prevent CIVO (1/6), obs-decoder SGS degrades critic calibration across all seeds: by 215K, all four Walker seeds reach terminal $v/e$ ratios of $0.056$--$0.14$, including seed~1 (the sole CIVO-free seed, eval 726 but value mean 41). The intervention trades overestimation for systematic underestimation, likely because detaching observation decoder gradients from $e_{\dt}$ damages the shared RSSM latent space that the critic relies on for value estimation. Seed~3 exhibits a fourth post-CIVO trajectory not observed in untreated seeds: latent onset (healthy through 105K), delayed collapse ($\nve = 6.8\times$ at 145K), partial policy recovery (eval 590 at 215K, 64\% of baseline) but persistent critic damage ($v/e = 0.14$), suggesting CIVO-induced representational harm may be irreversible even when the policy recovers (Appendix~\ref{sec:seed_divergence}).

